// Fasan Split – English texts of the guide (see tutorial_de.dart). MPL-2.0
const Map<String, String> tutorialEn = {
  'tutorial.title': 'Guide',
  'tutorial.intro': 'How to split bills with Fasan Split: scan a receipt, add people, assign items, settle up.',
  'tutorial.idea.title': 'The idea',
  'tutorial.idea.body': 'You photograph the receipt, say who was there and tap who had what. The app calculates everything automatically. There is no account; everything stays on your device until you share it.',
  'tutorial.scan.title': 'Scan a receipt',
  'tutorial.scan.body': 'Tap the plus at the bottom right. Photograph the receipt with the camera, pick a photo or file from the gallery (several at once is fine) or choose “Without receipt” to enter it by hand. The app reads items and total itself.',
  'tutorial.check.title': 'Check',
  'tutorial.check.body': 'At the top of the bill are “What for” and the total; category, date and place open behind the grey line below. Compare total and items with the receipt. The receipt icon at the top shows the photo. Tap an item that is wrong to change it. Everything is saved right away; “Continue later” only closes the bill. The frame of items and bills shows how much is assigned: red open, amber partial, green complete. “Only open items” shows only what is still missing. The list is sorted by status, newest first within it; other sorts and filters are under the filter icon at the top right.',
  'tutorial.assign.title': 'Who was there, who had what',
  'tutorial.assign.body': 'Add the people under “Who was there?”. Pick a person and tap the items they had. If several share an item, assign it to several people. The app works out the shares.',
  'tutorial.paid.title': 'Who paid',
  'tutorial.paid.body': 'The “Paid by” card sits right above the items and counts like an item: red while nobody is chosen, green once it is clear who laid out the money. Tap it and pick the person. That decides who owes whom how much. In a group it shows as a row in the items view; the status buttons and the search (“beer”, “paid”) find it like an item. Your payment details stay on your device: whoever needs them asks via “Ask for payment details” in your profile, and you decide in the chat with “Send”. Pin what matters: “Pin” in a bill\'s ⋮ menu, or in an item\'s sheet. Pinned things rise to the top and only count on your device. In a bill\'s ⋮ menu, “Share as PDF” makes one page with all items, the total and each person\'s share – without the photo of the receipt.',
  'tutorial.group.title': 'Create a group',
  'tutorial.group.body': 'Tap “All groups” at the top left. In the window you pick a group or create one with “New group”, for example for a trip or a flat share; the search helps with many groups. With a group picked, the plus starts a new bill that lands right there. You can press and hold a bill and drag it onto “Group” at the bottom. “All” shows everything, “No group” only bills without a group. At the top of the group you see the number of bills, the total and the people. The frame shows how many items are done, in progress or open; the total opens the breakdown. The frame shows bills, total and people, also for “All groups”. The buttons below count items (done, in progress, open) and bills without a payer; tap one to show only those, tap again to switch it off. “Bills | Items” changes the view. Open, Archive and Trash are chosen with the symbol at the top right, sorting and category with the filter symbol, “Select” in the ⋮ menu. While selecting, “Send (N)” at the bottom sends the chosen bills or items to a chat; the app asks first, and you can undo for 10 seconds. In the “Items” view every item looks like in the bill, with the snippet from the receipt; tap it to change it right there. Search finds names, people, items and amounts, remembers your last searches and suggests a fix for typos; a hit opens the bill at that item. Every question mark opens an explanation.',
  'tutorial.invite.title': 'Invite people',
  'tutorial.invite.body': 'Open the group and tap the person icon at the top. Share the link or the code. Whoever opens it is in the group and sees the bills. With “Share live” everyone stays in sync.',
  'tutorial.together.title': 'Enter together',
  'tutorial.together.body': 'In a group anyone can enter for anyone. The app keeps calculating automatically. In the “Settlement” tab you already see who owes whom while you are still entering. You settle up once all bills are entered. To protect something, lock it with the padlock: an item in the item sheet, a whole bill in the menu (⋮). Then only you and the group admin can change it; notes still work. You can write a note on every item and pin a note on every bill (also from the list: ⋮ on the bill card → “Note on the bill”); search finds both. With “@Name” in the note of an item you mention someone. A tap in the news leads straight to the bill or the message. If someone enters an item for you only as “maybe”, you get a news entry and decide in the item sheet: “Accept” or “Decline”. Until then it does not count. For others you suggest in the item sheet: “Suggest for someone (maybe)”. Who may enter for you is set per member: tap a member, “May change my shares”: directly, ask first or not allowed. Want to show only some items? Open the item and tap “Send items …”, and they land in the chat as a card. Should not everyone in the group see a bill? Menu (⋮) → “Visible to everyone in the group” → “People on it only”: then only you and the people on the bill can read it. Whoever already had a copy keeps it, and it cannot be undone. When hiding you can tick “Keep amounts visible for everyone”: the others then see total, payer and amount per person (with a lock symbol), but no item names, photos or notes. Items from it cannot be sent to the chat. New people should not see old bills? When inviting: “Hide existing bills”. Under “Members” you can make your new bills in this group people-on-them-only from the start. Tap a person in the group (or the name at the top of a chat) to see their profile: whether they linked an account or are only a name, their balance from finished bills (marked “uncertain” when open bills or missing payers make it unsure), your shared groups and what they changed. Tap a person\'s balance to see how it comes about for that person only. In a person\'s profile you choose whether their entries about you apply at once, wait for you or are not allowed; in your own profile one switch covers everyone. If “Everybody is admin“ is off in the members list, you appoint admins in the profile; the founder can turn it on for everyone. Every person has a colour, initials and their own hatching, so people can be told apart without colour vision. In the chat the name above a message opens that person\'s profile; in the friends list ⋮ shows everything you can do with a friend. In the members list admins set under “Who may do what” whether only admins add bills, change them or write notes.',
  'tutorial.history.title': 'Balance and history',
  'tutorial.history.body': 'In the profile, “How your balance adds up” shows every bill with plus and minus. In the menu (⋮) of a bill, a group and in the profile you find the history: who changed what and how your balance moved. The “Balance” tab lists every change to your balance with its cause; tap a row to see who changed what (with the device), open the receipt or undo the change. If someone changed a bill, a counter on its thumbnail shows how much, and the top of the bill shows one line “New since your visit” that leads to the history. If a shared bill got mixed up, “Bring back an earlier state” at the top of the bill history restores a member\'s last state. In your own profile you can show your amount history to members (off by default); hidden bills never appear.',
  'tutorial.settle.title': 'Settle up',
  'tutorial.settle.body': 'Once all bills are in, the people icon at the top of the group shows who pays whom how much. Tap ⋮ on a bill and then “Settle” when it is paid. Settled bills go to the archive. Paid something in between or lent money? In the people window enter it with “Enter a payment or loan”; the balance changes at once.',
  'tutorial.account.title': 'Account, devices, sign out',
  'tutorial.account.body': 'In the profile under “Account and devices”: “Move to a new device” shows a code you scan on the other device with “Sign in with a device code”. Your 12 words (under “Words and key”, with copy) bring your account back without a second device. “Sign out” only affects this device and deletes nothing. “Delete account” applies to everyone and cannot be undone.',
  'tutorial.settings.title': 'Settings and backup',
  'tutorial.settings.body': 'There you find appearance, language, performance and this guide. If the app stutters, the “Performance test” under Diagnostics runs a measurement with made-up data and makes a report to share. You open the settings from your profile (picture at the top right), at its top right. In the profile you switch the stand-in: whether others may enter things for you. There you back up your data with “Save a backup”. In the browser, „Check for updates now“ shows the build of your page and reloads it when a newer one exists; your login stays.',
};
